  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted as already signed to the registered direction, so positive values support the registered hypothesis and negative values oppose it. Practical 10 percent thresholds used here are approximately USP7 0.0093, NFE2L2 0.0093, MDM2 0.0269, KRAS 0.0245, and RIT1 0.0256. H101 completes the TP53 loss and USP7 story by testing the KEAP1-intact complement. Its signed estimate is +0.804, interval +0.782 to +0.827, with cell sizes 321 and 1286; this is enormously above the USP7 threshold and, together with validated H12, accepted H25, H43, and non-Avana H85, supports the association independently of KEAP1 status. I accept and close H101. H40, H41, and H54 are complement robustness checks for KEAP1 loss and weaker NFE2L2 dependency in TP53-intact, KRAS-mutant, and EGFR-amplification-negative cells. Their signed estimates are +0.792, +0.805, and +0.793, with lower bounds +0.770, +0.767, and +0.771 respectively. These are far above the NFE2L2 threshold and are close to the previously validated effect size, so I accept and close all three. The CDKN2A-loss and MDM2 signal receives strong within-dataset robustness support. H97, the non-Avana TP53-intact subset, has signed estimate +0.130 and lower bound +0.040, above the MDM2 threshold despite small cell sizes 39 and 153. H98, the adenocarcinoma TP53-intact subset, has +0.103 and lower bound +0.057. H102, the low-9p21 copy-number stratum, has +0.112 and lower bound +0.062. Because the lower bounds all exceed the practical 10 percent threshold, I accept these as supportive in-dataset associations and close them. However, they are all subsets of the same supplied dataset, so independent validation is still needed for the main H96 claim; I request validation for H96. H103 tests MTAP co-loss within CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact cells. Its signed estimate is +0.065, interval -0.034 to +0.164. The interval crosses zero, includes subthreshold effects, and is very wide; the evidence is too imprecise to distinguish a clinically meaningful MTAP co-deletion effect from no effect. I keep H103 unresolved and deferred, and register broader MTAP comparisons as targeted follow-up proposals. The remaining new bypass tests are not supported. H99, STK11 loss among KEAP1-intact cells for weaker NFE2L2 dependency, is essentially null: -0.0017, interval -0.023 to +0.0195, so I reject and close it. H100, PIK3CA mutation for weaker KRAS dependency among KRAS-wildtype cells, is near null with opposite-signed point estimate, -0.0008, interval -0.026 to +0.0246; I reject and close it. H104, STK11 loss among KRAS-mutant cells for weaker KRAS dependency, has negative point estimate -0.0139 and interval -0.053 to +0.0256; the upper bound is only marginally around the KRAS threshold and the interval is dominated by zero and opposite-signed values, so there is no meaningful support and I reject and close it. H105, PIK3CA mutation for weaker RIT1 dependency among KRAS-wildtype cells, is near null with upper bound +0.0187 below the RIT1 threshold, so I reject and close it. These conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset, not causal claims or claims of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 appraise. Requested independent validation for H96, the main accepted in-dataset association: CDKN2A loss among TP53-intact cells with much stronger MDM2 dependency, signed discovery +0.119, interval +0.079 to +0.158. New within-dataset robustness supports this: H97 non-Avana +0.130, lower +0.040; H98 adenocarcinoma +0.103, lower +0.057; H102 low-9p21 copy stratum +0.112, lower +0.062. All lower bounds exceed MDM2 10 percent threshold. H101 accepted and closed: TP53 loss and weaker USP7 dependency in KEAP1-intact cells +0.804, lower +0.782; combined with H12 validation and H43/H85/H25 gives strong support. H40/H41/H54 accepted and closed: KEAP1 loss and weaker NFE2L2 dependency in TP53-intact, KRAS-mutant, and EGFR-amplification-negative cells, all far above threshold. H103 MTAP co-loss within CDKN2A-loss cells unresolved and deferred due wide interval crossing zero; registered MTAP overall and MTAP effect in CDKN2A-intact complement. Rejected and closed new bypass claims: H99 STK11/KEAP1-intact NFE2L2, H100 PIK3CA/KRAS-wildtype KRAS, H104 STK11/KRAS-mutant KRAS, H105 PIK3CA/KRAS-wildtype RIT1. Deferred low-priority active broad claims, leaving H42 active as a potentially high-value KEAP1 robustness check if analysis slots permit. Next priority is assess H96 validation; if validation interval remains above threshold, upgrade generalization within validation split, otherwise reassess H96 and the accepted status of subset robustness claims. If H96 validates, MTAP and 9p21 mechanism should only be interpreted with caution unless follow-up MTAP tests become precise.",
  "validate": "H96"
}

